sequenceDiagram
    %% Phase 7 — `rewind enrich TRACE` command sequence.
    %% Drives every span in a trace (or branch) through enrich_span.

    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant CLI as rewind cli
    participant Store as TraceStore
    participant ES as enrich_span()
    participant PQ as parse_quant()
    participant SV as sample_vram()
    participant Ops as NVIDIA-smi<br/>macmon · psutil

    U->>CLI: rewind enrich TRACE<br/>[--branch B] [--sample-vram]
    Note over CLI: resolve target spans<br/>(root branch vs B)
    CLI->>Store: get_trace(T) ⟵ branch_id=None<br/>else get_spans(T, branch_id=B)
    Store-->>CLI: list[Span]
    loop each span
        opt span.kind == LLM
            CLI->>ES: enrich_span(span,<br/>parse_quant=True,<br/>sample_gpu=flag)
            opt parse_model_quant=True
                ES->>PQ: parse_quant(span.model_name)
                Note over ES,PQ: preferred: rewind.local.quant attr<br/>(if already set, skip parse)
                PQ-->>ES: QuantInfo(label="q4_K_M", bits=4)
                ES->>ES: span.raw_attributes["rewind.local.quant"]=label
            end
            opt sample_gpu=True
                ES->>SV: sample_vram()
                SV->>Ops: probe nvidia-smi → asitop/macmon → psutil
                Ops-->>SV: vram_mib:int, gpu_pct:int | None
                SV-->>ES: VramSample(vram_mib, gpu_pct)
                ES->>ES: write vram_mib + gpu_pct attrs (if present)
            end
            ES-->>CLI: mutated span
        end
        CLI->>Store: insert_span(span, branch_id=B)<br/>(ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE)
    end
    Store-->>CLI: ok
    CLI-->>U: "enriched N spans, M had quant hint, K had VRAM sample"

    Note over U,Ops: Side-effect free — reads source attrs,<br/>only writes under rewind.local.* namespace.<br/>No schema migration required.
